The application is a menu item target like any other, and AppKit answers for it.

CMake's menus did not open. Clicking File highlighted nothing and dropped nothing down, with no
error a user could see, because -[NSApplication validateMenuItem:] did not exist: Qt targets menu
items at NSApp, sends the validation, and the unrecognized selector RAISED inside the event loop,
which caught it and lost the whole menu-open event with it. This is the same shape as the six
selectors in patch 0054 and it is worth stating as a rule: a selector an application sends DURING
event handling must not raise, because the toolkit swallows the event whole.

It was NOT our own validation doing the sending. NSMenu.m already guards with respondsToSelector,
and CIDER_TRACE_MENU confirms it: across a File menu click the 23 items it validates target QNSView
and QCocoaMenuLoader, never the application. The send comes from Qt, which is entitled to it because
macOS answers.

The answer is the ordinary default for a validation with no opinion: whether the receiver can
perform the action at all. Returning a flat YES would enable items the application cannot run.

MEASURED: the File menu now opens, File highlights, and Reload Cache and Delete Cache are listed.
The selector count in the log goes from 2 to 0, and there are no exceptions and no faults.

--- a/AppKit/NSApplication.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSApplication.m
@@ -573,6 +573,17 @@
     return NO;
 }
 
+/* THE APPLICATION IS A MENU ITEM TARGET LIKE ANY OTHER, and AppKit answers for it. Qt asks NSApp
+ * to validate items it has targeted there, and with no implementation the send RAISED, the event
+ * loop caught it, and CMake's File menu simply did not open: no dropdown, no error a user could
+ * see. The answer macOS gives is the ordinary default for a validation with no opinion, which is
+ * whether the receiver can perform the action at all. Task #227. */
+- (BOOL) validateMenuItem: (NSMenuItem *) item {
+    SEL action = [item action];
+
+    return action != NULL && [self respondsToSelector: action];
+}
+
